Industrial Chemical Technology I — Adebayo, NOUN (@ic-noun-one: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_2026VMVXVJQGK3WTH1P17FE8T9
Kolawole Sunday Adebayo, course developer; Folahan Adekola, course editor. Industrial Chemical Technology I, CHM316, National Open University of Nigeria, printed 2012. [Official complete 56-page course text](https://nou.edu.ng/coursewarecontent/CHM%20316%20-%20INDUSTRIAL%20CHEMICAL%20TECHNOLOGY%20I.pdf) · [University courseware catalogue and use terms](https://nou.edu.ng/ecourseware-faculty-of-sciences/).

Read the complete course guide and study units as a first orientation to transformations, operations, heat/mass transfer, equipment, and the purposes of industrial chemistry. Work the questions and independently derive numerical claims. The later university courses, full reactor book, technical process books, and primary methods provide substantially greater depth.

The university explicitly permits reading/downloading its educational courseware and prohibits commercial/financial use outside education; the PDF states all rights reserved. This is free authorized educational access, not a blanket open licence. Author, date, contents, full-text route, and notices were checked on 29 October 2026. Historical prices, methods, references, and simplified explanations need their actual context. Nothing is mirrored.

**Return:** [Industrial chemistry sources — whole books, courses, technical methods and primary evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3084780FHMK499ZDAW07TYA3TQ).
